According to [hang-stats](https://fqueze.github.io/hang-stats) mozilla::dom::ScreenOrientation::ShouldResistFingerprinting() is consistently found in hangs every day.

The [content of this function](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/352b525ab841278cd9b3098343f655ef85933544/dom/base/ScreenOrientation.cpp#572) is

```
bool ScreenOrientation::ShouldResistFingerprinting() const {
  bool resist = false;
  if (nsCOMPtr<nsPIDOMWindowInner> owner = GetOwner()) {
    resist = nsContentUtils::ShouldResistFingerprinting(owner->GetDocShell());
  }
  return resist;
}
```

Which seems pretty tight. The call to ShouldResistFingerprinting() inside the function cascades down to several other ShouldResistFingerprinting() functions, some which are inlined I'm sure, but [the more complicated one](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/352b525ab841278cd9b3098343f655ef85933544/dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp#2208) seems unlikely to be inlined...

`CheckReturn` validates the return type while the function is still active, which isn't spec compliant, because the validation should actually happen after leaving the function body. See [10.2.2 [[Construct]], step 12](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-function-objects-construct-argumentslist-newtarget).

